{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHabiroInfiniteRigidity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHabiroInfiniteRigidity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHabiroRootFamily"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHabiroInfiniteRigidity.two_roots_insufficient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHabiroInfiniteRigidity.two_roots_insufficient","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHabiroInfiniteRigidity.lean#L95-L112","doc":"**Two roots are insufficient (the Σ(2,3,5) slice alone does not pin the value\nmap).** For any two distinct fibre points `a ≠ b` and any value-map polynomial `V`,\nthere is a *different* polynomial `W ≠ V` agreeing with `V` at both points\n(`W = V + (X−a)(X−b)`).  So the two-flat-connection agreement of `KeystoneLRAmplitudeReal`\n(#4365) cannot alone force `bwS0 = V` — brackets the residual `bwsc` from below:\n2 roots fail, the infinite family (`eq_of_habiro_root_agreement`) succeeds, so the\nopen work is exactly *extending the WRT agreement from the Σ(2,3,5) slice toward the\nfull root family*. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHabiroInfiniteRigidity.eq_of_habiro_root_agreement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHabiroInfiniteRigidity.eq_of_habiro_root_agreement","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHabiroInfiniteRigidity.lean#L80-L93","doc":"**Habiro all-roots agreement forces equality (no degree bound).** If the\ngauge-row polynomial `bwPoly` agrees with the value-map polynomial `valPoly` at every\nfold value `2cos(π/(N+2))` (the full fibre-root family), then `bwPoly = valPoly` —\nhence they agree at the substrate `t₀`.  The bounded-degree hypothesis (bwsd) is\ndissolved by the infinitude of the root family; the sole residual is the agreement\nitself (bwsc / WRT = modular-data). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHabiroInfiniteRigidity.foldValues_infinite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHabiroInfiniteRigidity.foldValues_infinite","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHabiroInfiniteRigidity.lean#L74-L78","doc":"The fibre-root fold values `{2cos(π/(N+2)) : N ∈ ℕ}` form an **infinite** set —\nthe WRT/Habiro all-levels root family. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHabiroInfiniteRigidity.foldOne_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHabiroInfiniteRigidity.foldOne_injective","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHabiroInfiniteRigidity.lean#L44-L72","doc":"The single-index fibre fold family `N ↦ 2cos(π/(N+2))` is injective: the angles\n`π/(N+2)` are distinct in `(0, π]` and `cos` is injective there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHabiroInfiniteRigidity.eq_of_infinite_agreement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHabiroInfiniteRigidity.eq_of_infinite_agreement","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHabiroInfiniteRigidity.lean#L37-L42","doc":"**Infinite-root rigidity.** If two real polynomials agree on an infinite set of\npoints, they are equal.  (A nonzero polynomial has finitely many roots.) ","signatureChunk":0}]}